        "original_id": "cf76b654-6aae-51a8-8ba6-831641be8890",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles II of England, Charles Lennox\n- Titles: Duke of Richmond, Duke of Lennox\n- Places: England, Scotland, Ireland\n\nFacts:\n- Charles II of England was born on 29 May 1630 and died on 6 February 1685.\n- Charles II was king of Scotland from 1649 until his deposition in 1651.\n- Charles II was king of England, Scotland and Ireland from the restoration of the monarchy in 1660 until his death.\n- In 1675, King Charles II created his illegitimate son Charles Lennox Duke of Richmond on 9 August 1675.\n- In 1675, King Charles II created Charles Lennox Duke of Lennox on 9 September 1675.\n- The dukedoms of Richmond and Lennox have been held concurrently by Charles Lennox's descendants since their creation in 1675.",
